   "source": [
    "\"Natural product databases were integrated from three sources. NPASS 3.0 provided 203,390 natural products with associated bioactivity records, plant species annotations, and cross-references to external databases. COCONUT (October 2024 release) contributed 695,133 structurally diverse natural products with pre-computed physicochemical descriptors and NP Classifier pathway annotations. AfroDb (April 2026) was used as an annotation layer: compounds in COCONUT were flagged as African natural products via the embedded collections field, while NPASS compounds were cross-referenced against AfroDb via InChIKey connectivity layer matching. Compounds with non-standard valences, permanent charges, or mixture representations (n = 1,415; 0.7%) were excluded from NPASS prior to analysis. Physicochemical descriptors for NPASS compounds were computed using RDKit; COCONUT descriptors were used as pre-computed by the COCONUT pipeline. The final integrated resource comprised 201,975 annotated NPASS compounds and 695,133 COCONUT compounds, together representing the primary chemical space for downstream QSAR-guided virtual screening.\""
